Chapter: SelectorNoField

 A dot that opens a selector must be followed by a field name, and saying
 so is the whole point of this test. Until this was fixed the
 parser returned ExprOk here WITHOUT consuming the dot, so the statement
 loop met the same token forever: the heap climbed, the stack sank a
 gigabyte, and the compile double-faulted with no diagnostic at all.

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line "codex"
   .
  end
